{#
  Section: owns the macro rhythm. Vertical padding (the section-level step of
  the spacing scale, and the ONLY place that step is allowed, never
  component-internal) plus the 1120px container, both applied automatically.

  py-24 is Tailwind's 96px step. The container it wraps is .cs-container, not
  max-w-main plus px-8; see components/container.css for why.

  `pad` EXISTS BECAUSE THE RHYTHM IS MOVING TO 88px AND THIS MACRO IS SHARED.
  Five pages call it, so flipping the default would move every one of them in a
  commit meant to touch one. A page that has been reset to the new rhythm passes
  pad="py-22"; everything else keeps the 96px default untouched.

  IT IS AN ARGUMENT RATHER THAN A CSS OVERRIDE ON PURPOSE. py-24 is a Tailwind
  utility, and utilities sit in a later cascade layer than @layer components, so
  a page stylesheet cannot beat it. Overriding from CSS looks like it works
  until someone checks the computed value.

  The default goes to py-22 and this parameter is removed once every page has
  moved. If you are reading this and no caller passes pad, that is the signal.

  `deep` paints the one ink pane. design.md section 1: MAX ONE deep pane per
  view. Buttons inside a deep section must use variant="deep", and the wordmark
  its --on-deep modifier, or they render ink-on-ink and vanish.

  Usage:
    {% raw %}{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
    {% call section(deep=true) %}...{% endcall %}{% endraw %}
#}
{% macro section(deep=false, class="", containerClass="", id="", label="", pad="py-24") %}
<section{% if id %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}{% if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %} class="{{ pad }}{{ " bg-ink text-paper" if deep }}{{ " " + class if class }}">
  <div class="cs-container{{ " " + containerClass if containerClass }}">
    {{ caller() }}
  </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
